	<!--
	<skill id="item1">
		<skillReference id="skill1" /> Type is ID of Skill defined in Skills tag
		<requirements>
			<minimumLevel level="1" /> Minimum required Player Level
			<skillPointType type="bronze" /> Skillpoint Type (reference to skillPoint ID in skillPoints) required to spend for skill
			<unlockedSkills> Other skills where MAX points are required to be spent before item is available
				<skillReference id="item1" /> Reference to another item inside the skilltree
			</unlockedSkills>
			<pointsAccumulated amount="5"> Amount of points that has to be spent in the following other skilltree items
				<skillReference id="item1" /> Reference to another item insider the skilltree
				<skillReference id="item2" />
			</pointsAccumulated>
		</requirements>
		<levels> Unlock levels for skilltree item, every level equals another skillpoint that needs to be spent, different values per unlock level can be assigned to the available manipulators
			<level> Levels are sorted, first sibling stand for 1st level, second sibling for 2nd etc.
				<param targetModifierId="modifier1" name="param1" value="10" /> pass parameter with name "param1" and value "10" to modifier "modifer1"
			</level>
			<level>
				<param targetModifierId="modifier2" name="param1" value="20" />
			</level>
		</levels>
		<layout>  Specific rendering data, required for the client to display the skilltree
			<icon name="icon1.png" /> Icon to display for skill
			<position x="1" y="0" /> Rendering position inside slot matrix, x=0 equals left-most col, y=0 equals bottom-most row
			<arrows> Arrow definitions
				<arrow type="TOP_1_UP" /> Arrow definition syntax: <Arrow Position from current item>_<Amount of Rows the arrow is skipping>_<Directions the Arrow is pointing towards>
				<arrow type="LEFT_2_UP" />
				<arrow type="RIGHT_1_UP" />
				
				<arrow type="TOP_1_UPRIGHT" />
			</arrows>
		</layout>
	</skill>

{0} = Chance / modifierChance
{1} = value
{2} = multiplier(*100)
{3} = Adder

	-->
	
